{"case_id":"seeded-off-by-one-pagination","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Offset calculation in page_bounds is incorrect for 1-indexed pagination.","category":"correctness","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/pagination.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":6,"end_line":9},"explanation":"For 1-indexed pagination, page=1 should have an offset of 0. However, `page_bounds` calculates `offset = page * page_size`. For `page=1` and `page_size=20`, `offset` becomes `1 * 20 = 20`, skipping the first 20 items on the first page. It should be `(page - 1) * page_size`.","suggested_fix":"Change offset calculation to `offset = (page - 1) * page_size`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O6","note":"offset is calculated as page * page_size instead of (page - 1) * page_size, causing page 1 to start at index page_size instead of 0.","ref":"head","path":"app/pagination.py","start_line":6,"end_line":9,"snippet":"def page_bounds(page: int, page_size: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Return (limit, offset) for the 1-indexed `page`.\"\"\"\n    offset = page * page_size\n    return page_size, offset","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O10","note":"items list endpoint calls page_bounds and passes the resulting offset to SQL LIMIT/OFFSET query.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/items.py","start_line":21,"end_line":21,"snippet":"    limit, offset = page_bounds(page, page_size)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"off-by-one","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":7440,"output_tokens":415,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":2,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":2,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":3.16,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-path-traversal-attachments","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Path traversal vulnerability in attachment download endpoint allowing arbitrary file read.","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/attachments.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":17,"end_line":17},"explanation":"The `get_attachment` endpoint uses `os.path.join(ATTACHMENT_DIR, filename)` without validating or sanitizing `filename`. An attacker can pass directory traversal sequences (such as `../`) in the `filename` parameter to read arbitrary files accessible to the application process, bypassing the intended attachment directory restriction.","suggested_fix":"Use `safe_join` from `app.storage` (or similar path validation ensuring the resolved path is within `ATTACHMENT_DIR`) instead of `os.path.join`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O6","note":"os.path.join with unsanitized filename allows path traversal sequences like ../.. to escape ATTACHMENT_DIR","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/attachments.py","start_line":17,"end_line":17,"snippet":"    path = os.path.join(ATTACHMENT_DIR, filename)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"traversal","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":25997,"output_tokens":424,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":4017},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":6,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":6,"tool_calls":5,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":53.902,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-sql-injection-search","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in item search endpoint via unescaped query parameter f-string interpolation","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/items.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":36},"explanation":"The search endpoint constructs the SQL query using an f-string with `term` directly interpolated into the query string (`WHERE name LIKE '%{term}%'`). Since user-controlled query parameter `q` is interpolated without sanitization or parameterization, an attacker can perform SQL injection attacks.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries instead of f-string interpolation, e.g. `db.query(\"SELECT id, name, price FROM items WHERE name LIKE ? ORDER BY name LIMIT 50\", (f\"%{term}%\",))`","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O10","note":"SQL query is built using f-string interpolation of user-supplied `term` without query parameters","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/items.py","start_line":33,"end_line":36,"snippet":"    rows = db.query(\n        f\"SELECT id, name, price FROM items WHERE name LIKE '%{term}%' ORDER BY name LIMIT 50\"\n    )\n    return Response.json([dict(row) for row in rows])","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O13","note":"Database docstring explicitly specifies to always pass values as parameters, never in the SQL text","ref":"head","path":"app/db.py","start_line":1,"end_line":1,"snippet":"\"\"\"Thin wrapper around sqlite3. Always pass values as parameters, never in the SQL text.\"\"\"","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":20454,"output_tokens":436,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":6029},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":5,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":5,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":52.942,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-gen-salt-random","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Using random.choices instead of secrets.choice for generating password salts and security tokens weakens cryptographic security.","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":34,"end_line":34},"explanation":"The `gen_salt` function is used for generating cryptographic salts (for password hashing via `generate_password_hash`) and security tokens (for debugger console secrets). Switching from `secrets.choice` to `random.choices` replaces cryptographically secure random selection (`secrets`) with Python's standard `random` module, which uses the Mersenne Twister and is predictable. This compromises the cryptographic security of password hashes and session/debugger tokens.","suggested_fix":"Revert to secrets.choice or use secrets.randbelow / secrets.token_bytes with base64/hex encoding.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O4","note":"random.choices uses the standard Mersenne Twister random number generator (random module) rather than cryptographically secure pseudorandom number generation (secrets module).","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":34,"end_line":34,"snippet":"    return \"\".join(random.choices(SALT_CHARS, k=length))","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"Replaces cryptographically secure secrets.choice with insecure random.choices.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":34,"end_line":34,"snippet":"    return \"\".join(random.choices(SALT_CHARS, k=length))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"predictable-salt","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":15987,"output_tokens":446,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":2011},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":4,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":4,"tool_calls":3,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":8.715,"error":null}
